              %p
                Finally, these adjunctions are a sequence of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalences"} Quillen equivalences
                with respect to the:
              %table
                %thead
                  %tr
                    %th
                    %th
                    %th
                %tbody
                  %tr
                    %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} classical model structure on topological spaces
                    %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+D-topological+spaces"} model structure on D-topological spaces
                    %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+diffeological+spaces"} model structure on diffeological spaces
              %blockquote
                %p
                  Caution: There was a gap in the original proof that
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi DTopologicalSpaces
                          %msub
                            %mo ≃
                            %mi Quillen
                          %mi DiffeologicalSpaces
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} DTopologicalSpaces \simeq_{Quillen} DiffeologicalSpaces
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a{:href => "model+structure+on+diffeological+spaces#References"} here
            %p
              Essentially these adjunctions and their properties are observed in
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "diffeological+space#SYH10"} Shimakawa, Yoshida &amp; Haraguchi 2010, Prop. 3.1, Prop. 3.2, Lem. 3.3
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "D-topology#CSW13"} Christensen, Sinnamon &amp; Wu 2014, Sec. 3.2
              %a{:href => "#model+structure+on+Delta-generated+topological+spaces#Haraguchi13"} Haraguchi 13, Thm. 3.3
              (on the left) and
              %a{:href => "model+structure+on+diffeological+spaces#HaraguchiShimakawa13"} Haraguchi-Shimakawa 13, Sec. 7
              (on the right).
            .proof
              %h6#proof Proof
              %p
                We spell out the existence of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+adjunction"} idempotent adjunction
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:DeltaGeneratedSpacesInIdempotentAdjunction"} (2)
              %p
                First, to see we have an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Dtplg
                        %mo ⊣
                        %mi Cdfflg
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Dtplg \dashv Cdfflg
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a{:href => "adjoint+functor#eq:HomIsomorphismForAdjointFunctors"} here
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi DiffeologicalSpaces
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in DiffeologicalSpaces
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Y
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi TopologicalSpaces
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \in TopologicalSpaces
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)_s
                for the underlying sets. Then a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
                of the form
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi Dtplg
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi Y
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      f \;\colon\; Dtplg(X) \longrightarrow Y
                      \\,,
              %p
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi s
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi s
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi Y
                        %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_s \colon X_s \to Y_s
                of the underlying
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
                such that for every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subset"} open subset
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msub
                        %mi Y
                        %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \subset Y_s
                and every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
                of the form
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \colon \mathbb{R}^n \to X
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preimage"} preimage
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi s
                      %mo ∘
                      %msub
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mi s
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f_s \circ \phi_s)^{-1}(A) \subset \mathbb{R}^n
                is open. But this means equivalently that for every such
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ϕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi ϕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \circ \phi
                is
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_s
                constitutes a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi f
                          %mo ˜
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi X
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi Cdfflg
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widetilde f \;\colon\; X \longrightarrow Cdfflg(Y)
              %p
                In summary, we thus have a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-sets"} hom-sets
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi Hom
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi Dtplg
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi X
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo ,
                              %mi Y
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mo ≃
                            %mtd
                              %mi Hom
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi X
                              %mo ,
                              %mi Cdfflg
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi Y
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi f
                                %mi s
                            %mtd
                              %mo ↦
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mover
                                %mi f
                                %mo ˜
                              %msub
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mi s
                              %mo =
                              %msub
                                %mi f
                                %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      Hom( Dtplg(X), Y )
                      \&amp;\simeq&amp;
                      Hom(X, Cdfflg(Y))
                      \\\
                      f_s &amp;\mapsto&amp; (\widetilde f)_s = f_s
                      }
              %p
                given simply as the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+function"} identity
                on the underlying
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
                of underlying sets. This makes it immediate that this hom-isomorphism is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+bijection"} natural
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
                and this establishes the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
              %p
                Next, to see that the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-topological+spaces"} D-topological spaces
                are the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+point+of+an+adjunction"} fixed points
                of this adjunction, we apply the above
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+bijection"} natural bijection
                on hom-sets to the case
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi Ho
                              %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                              %mi Dtplg
                              %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                              %mi Cdfflg
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi Z
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                              %mo ,
                              %mi Y
                              %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mo ≃
                            %mtd
                              %mi Hom
                              %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                              %mi Cdfflg
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi Z
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo ,
                              %mi Cdfflg
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi Y
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mi ϵ
                                %mi Z
                              %msub
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mi s
                            %mtd
                              %mo ↦
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} id
                              %msub
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      Ho\Big( Dtplg\big(Cdfflg(Z)\big), Y\Big)
                      \&amp;\simeq&amp;
                      Hom\big(Cdfflg(Z), Cdfflg(Y)\big)
                      \\\
                      (\epsilon_Z)_s &amp;\mapsto&amp; (\mathrm{id})_s
                      }
              %p
                to find that the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/counit+of+the+adjunction"} counit of the adjunction
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Dtplg
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                      %mi Cdfflg
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi ϵ
                            %mi X
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      Dtplg\big(Cdfflg(X)\big)
                      \\overset{\epsilon_X}{\longrightarrow}
                      X
              %p
                is given by the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+function"} identity function
                on the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying+sets"} underlying sets
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi ϵ
                          %mi X
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi s
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi id
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi s
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\epsilon_X)_s = id_{(X_s)}
              %p
                Therefore
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi η
                        %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_X
                is an
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_s
                with respect to the topology on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                are precisely those with respect to the topology on
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Dtplg
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                        %mi Cdfflg
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Dtplg\big(Cdfflg(X)\big)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                coincide with those whose pre-images under all continuous functions
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \colon \mathbb{R}^n \to X
                are open. This means equivalently that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                is a D-topological space.
              %p
                Finally, to see that we have an
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+adjunction"} idempotent adjunction
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "idempotent+adjunction#EquivalentConditionsForIdempotency"} this Prop.
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonad"} comonad
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Dtplg
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi Cdfflg
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi TopologicalSpaces
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi TopologicalSpaces
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      Dtplg \circ Cdfflg
                      \\;\colon\;
                      TopologicalSpaces \longrightarrow TopologicalSpaces
              %p
                is an
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+comonad"} idempotent comonad
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Dtplg
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi Cdfflg
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %mi Dtplg
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mi η
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mi Cdfflg
                      %mi Dtplg
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi Cdfflg
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi Dtplg
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi Cdfflg
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      Dtplg \circ Cdfflg
                      \\overset{
                      Dtplg \cdot \eta \cdot Cdfflg
                      }{\longrightarrow}
                      Dtplg \circ Cdfflg \circ Dtplg \circ Cdfflg
              %p
                is a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ϵ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction+unit"} adjunction unit
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi η
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+function"} identity function
                on the underlying sets. Therefore, this being a natural isomorphism is equivalent to the operation of passing to the D-topological refinement of the topology of a topological space being an idempotent operation, which is clearly the case.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorification"} categorification
                of the notion of idempotent adjunction is that of
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax-idempotent+2-adjunction"} lax-idempotent 2-adjunction
            %li
              %p
                In an
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+triple"} adjoint triple
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+pairs"} adjoint pairs
                is idempotent if and only if the other one is; see
                %a{:href => "adjoint+triple#Idempotent"} there
                for more.
          %h2#references References
          %p The characterization of idempotent adjunctions is proven/due to:
          %ul
            %li#MacDonaldStone82
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+L.+MacDonald"}> John L. MacDonald
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Arthur+L.+Stone"} Arthur L. Stone
              = succeed "," do
                %em The tower and regular decomposition
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item/?id=CTGDC_1982__23_2_197_0"} numdam:CTGDC_1982__23_2_197_0
          %p Textbook accounts:
          %ul
            %li#Grandis21
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marco+Grandis"}> Marco Grandis
              , Section 3.8 in:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Category Theory and Applications: A Textbook for Beginners
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/12253"} doi:10.1142/12253
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              Alessandro Ardizzoni, José Gómez-Torrecillas, Claudia Menini, Prop. 1.3 in:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Monadic Decompositions and Classical Lie Theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1203.2881"} arXiv:1203.2881
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10485-013-9326-7"} doi:10.1007/s10485-013-9326-7
          %p
            The
            %a{:href => "#BetweenTopologicalAndDiffeologicalSpaces"} example of D-topological spaces
            inside
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+spaces"} diffeological spaces
            is due to:
          %ul
            %li#SYH10
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kazuhisa+Shimakawa"}> Kazuhisa Shimakawa
              , K. Yoshida,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tadayuki+Haraguchi"} Tadayuki Haraguchi
              = succeed "," do
                %em Homology and cohomology via enriched bifunctors
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1010.3336"} arXiv:1010.3336
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2206/kyushujm.72.239"} doi:10.2206/kyushujm.72.239
          %p
            The example
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CoCommaAdjunction"}
            of the (co)comma adjunction is also mentioned in:
          %ul
            %li#Shulman16
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"}> Mike Shulman
              , reply
              %a{:href => "https://mathoverflow.net/a/247311/381"} MO:a/247311/381
              (2016) to: “An ‘explicit’ description of cocomma categories?”
